# RunPod Cost Guardrail

**Any RunPod MCP call that incurs cost or changes infrastructure state requires TWO explicit in-chat confirmations before invoking.**

## Cost / state-changing (double-confirm required)
`create-pod`, `start-pod`, `update-pod`, `create-network-volume`, `update-network-volume`, `create-endpoint`, `update-endpoint`, `run-endpoint`, `runsync-endpoint`

## Destructive / data-loss (double-confirm required)
`delete-pod`, `delete-network-volume`, `delete-endpoint`, `delete-template`

## Single ack (saves money)
`stop-pod` — encourage this; idle pods still bill.

## Read-only (no confirm needed)
`list-pods`, `get-pod`, `list-gpu-types`, `list-data-centers`, `list-templates`, `list/get-network-volume`, `list/get-endpoint`, `endpoint-health`, `get-job-status`

**Confirm flow:** (1) state exactly what will be created and the $/hr → "confirm?"; (2) after yes → "final confirm — provisioning now?"; only then invoke.
Also remind user to `stop-pod` when done. Source: `docs/claude/memory/runpod-cost-guardrail.md`
